History on the Himalayas

On 27 May 2025, history was etched on the slopes of Mt Everest as the Indian Army Adventure Wing achieved the Guinness World Record for the largest expeditionary force to summit the world’s highest peak — 49 climbers (22 Indian Army & 27 Sherpas).

Part of the Indian Army’s Silver Jubilee Everest Expedition, led by Lt Col Manoj Joshi, this extraordinary feat stands as a testament to courage, teamwork, and unwavering leadership in the harshest environment on Earth.

A landmark achievement reflecting the Indian Army’s spirit of adventure and excellence beyond the battlefield.

