In another landmark achievement, #CommandHospital Chandimandir, continuing its successful Bone Marrow Transplant programme, has performed its first Autologous Bone Marrow Transplant for a patient with Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma. The procedure involved the critical step of stem cell cryopreservation, undertaken by Dept of Transfusion Medicine, PGIMER.

Since the inauguration of the state-of-the-art Hematology Centre on 10 May 2025 by Lt Gen #ManojKumarKatiyar, PVSM, UYSM, AVSM, Army Commander, Western Command, the hospital has successfully conducted four transplants for Multiple Myeloma and one for Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma, reaffirming its commitment to delivering world-class healthcare.

