In a remarkable life-saving medical intervention, specialists at Army Institute of Cardio-Thoracic Sciences (#AICTS), Pune successfully treated the wife of a veteran suffering from advanced oesophageal cancer that had created a dangerous passage between her food pipe and airway (Tracheoesophageal fistula) leading to critical breathing complications.

Using ECMO support,the multidisciplinary team performed a rare and highly complex airway intervention with deployment of Self Expanding Metallic Inverted Y- Stent in the air passage, restoring her airway and giving a new lease of life.

The successful treatment reflects the Indian Army’s advanced medical capability and unwavering commitment towards the welfare of veterans and their families.

