Lt Gen Dhiraj Seth, PVSM, UYSM, AVSM, General Officer Commanding-in-Chief, addressed All Ranks of #SouthernCommand on the eve of relinquishing his command.

Commending all ranks for their steadfast professionalism and commitment during #OperationSindoor, the Army Commander underscored Southern Command’s progress under the #DecadeOfTransformation through  enhanced #Jointness, induction of modern technology and platforms, raising of new operational structures and incorporating innovative Tactics, Techniques and Procedures (#TTPs). He noted that sustained capability development and training across the Desert, Rann, Creek and Coastal Sectors have reinforced the Command’s combat edge for modern battlefields. 

In his address, the Army Commander reiterated five enduring ‘𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐬 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐚𝐥𝐥 𝐒𝐨𝐥𝐝𝐢𝐞𝐫𝐬’ : 
- To know one’s operational task with complete clarity and remain unwaveringly focused towards its execution; 
- To uphold, in every action, the honour,  pride and glory of the unit one serves;
- To care for juniors, respect seniors and preserve the camaraderie that forms the bedrock of the #IndianArmy;
- To remain physically fit and mentally robust as the foundation of a battle-ready force;
- To always remain conscious that, a soldier represents the Indian Army and its proud traditions in all his actions.

The Army Commander expressed complete confidence that Southern Command remains future-ready, adaptable and fully prepared to prosecute Multi-Domain operations across the full spectrum of modern conflict to defend the sovereignty of the nation

