A rare feat of global cardiac excellence in uniform.

Doctors at Army Institute of Cardiothoracic Sciences (AICTS), #Pune have successfully treated four patients with coronary stent infection and aneurysmal dilatation of the coronary artery following PCI—an ultra-rare complication, with only about 40 cases reported worldwide.

The patients, who had undergone prior treatment at civil and private hospitals across the country, were managed surgically through extraction/exclusion of the infected coronary stent aneurysm and bypass grafting distal to the affected segment, resulting in successful resolution of this complex iatrogenic complication.

This landmark achievement reflects the exceptional cardiac surgical expertise, advanced critical care capability and clinical excellence of the Armed Forces Medical Services.

