Turning Loss into Life through Precision, Compassion and Medical Excellence.

At Command Hospital, #SouthernCommand, #Pune, a brave soul became a silent saviour through organ donation.

In a remarkable display of meticulous surgical planning, clinical excellence and seamless execution, the organ retrieval was carried out with precision under the aegis of AORTA (Armed Forces Organ Retrieval & Transplantation Authority).

The liver was swiftly transported through a green corridor to Army Hospital (R&R), Delhi, while the donated kidney was successfully transplanted at Command Hospital, Pune, giving a retired soldier a renewed lease of life. 

Enabled by close coordination among HQ Southern Command, the Indian Air Force and Pune Police, the mission was executed with precision and timeliness, exemplifying seamless inter-agency synergy and the spirit of #MilitaryCivilFusion.

The mission reflects the exceptional professionalism, coordination and humanitarian commitment of the Army Medical Corps.

