#SailIndia2026 unfurls at the iconic Girgaon Chowpatty, igniting India’s high-performance sailing campaign on the road to the #2026AsianGames in Nagoya, Japan.

Bringing together nearly 150 of the nation’s finest sailors from 18 clubs and institutions, the Asian Games Selection Trials–II are a true test of skill, endurance and tactical mastery across Olympic and International classes. With cumulative points across three trials determining the final squad, every race carries the weight of national ambition.

Beyond elite competition, the championship reflects a larger vision strengthening India’s sailing ecosystem by nurturing young talent through grassroots initiatives in collaboration with the BMC and the Army Sailing School. Building on the momentum of India’s historic medal haul at the Hangzhou 2023 Asian Games, Sail India 2026 sends a clear message: India is ready to set the pace and make waves in Asian sailing.

