#OperationNetra 1.0 was conducted at Army General Hospital, #Leh from 26–30 April 2026, during which over 200 #Cataract patients from remote, high-altitude border villages of Ladakh (ranging between 9,000 and 15,000 feet) underwent successful surgeries, restoring their vision. Over the past three months, the #IndianArmy organised eye camps across #Tangtse, #Chushul, #Nyoma, #NubraValley and #Kargil providing quality eye care to more than 950 local residents and identifying patients in need of surgical intervention.

Shri Vinai Kumar Saxena, Hon’ble Lieutenant Governor #Ladakh, graced the closing ceremony at Rinchen Auditorium, #Leh and expressed heartfelt gratitude to the Indian Army on behalf of the people of Ladakh.

Lt Gen Pratik Sharma, #ArmyCdrNC, appreciated one of its kind initiatives at the most inhospitable terrain & climatic conditions towards #Nation Building through #Synergised
efforts by the team of Ophthalmologists from Army Hospital (R&R), Delhi  & SNM Hospital, Leh.

