#30May1999

"What I did at Chorbat La was my duty, not something extraordinary."

Major Sonam Wangchuk and the brave men of 3 Ladakh Scouts etched their names in history during the Battle of Chorbat La in Batalik Sector.

Battling sub-zero temperatures, snow blizzards, enemy fire and impossible terrain, Maj Wangchuk led from the front to establish observation posts at Sonam-I and Sonam-II, eliminating the enemy and denying Pakistani troops control of the ridgeline on the Ladakh Range.

India remembers with pride and gratitude. 🇮🇳

