Multi-Speciality Medical Camp : Nimu, Ladakh

A Multi-Speciality Medical Camp was conducted at Nimu, Ladakh on 16 May 2026 with participation of 18 civilian doctors from Maharashtra specialising in Medicine, Surgery, Paediatrics, Gynaecology, Ophthalmology, Dermatology, Orthopaedics and Dental Surgery.

In remote high-altitude regions where access to specialised healthcare remains limited, the initiative extended medical care to over 300 beneficiaries. The camp catered to 60 Ex-Servicemen and their families, while 223 civilians from remote villages benefitted from specialist consultations and treatment, reaffirming the Indian Army’s enduring bond with the people of Ladakh.

The initiative reaffirmed the Indian Army’s commitment towards the well-being of veterans, serving personnel and civilians residing in the remote frontiers of Ladakh.

