Medical Camp: Ladakh

On the occasion of Mother’s Day, Fire and Fury Corps organised a Medical Camp at the remote border villages of Urgo, Phobrang with a special focus on Maternal & Child Health Care. 

The camp included health check ups, awareness sessions and an informative lecture on maternal wellness, child nutrition and preventive healthcare. 

A 2-yr old Child with pulled elbow was also treated in camp with immediate relief and prevented potential life long disability. Two elderly patients with knee replacement surgery were also reviewed and one patient with painful hoarseness of voice was referred for evaluation of laryngeal tumour. 

The event reaffirmed the Army’s commitment towards the well being of border communities. 

