Road Safety & Traffic Discipline Capsule at Tangtse

Reaffirming its enduring commitment towards community outreach and public welfare, Fire & Fury Corps conducted a Road Safety & Traffic Discipline Capsule at Tangtse on 10 May 2026, in seamless coordination with the Civil and Military Police.

The awareness initiative witnessed spirited participation from over 60 drivers of the Ladakh Union and community members. It served as a vital platform to sensitise the populace on responsible driving practices, scrupulous adherence to traffic regulations, disciplined road conduct and the imperatives of safe mobility across the arduous mountainous terrain of Ladakh.

The programme was aimed at fostering heightened civic consciousness and nurturing a culture of prudence, restraint and collective responsibility amongst all road users, thereby contributing towards safer transit corridors in the strategically significant high altitude region.

The initiative was met with deep appreciation from the community.

