10TH TRI SERVICES ARMED FORCES VETERANS DAY: LADAKH

 10th ‘Tri Services Armed Forces Veterans Day’ was celebrated by Indian Army at Leh. Senior Military Officers and veterans paid homage to the fallen heroes by laying wreath at the Hall of Fame Memorial. 

More than 600 retired Armed Forces Personnel from Ladakh attended the event at Rinchen Auditorium in Leh. The Chief Guest, Lieutenant General Hitesh Bhalla, General Officer Commanding, Fire and Fury Corps addressed the veterans and thanked them for their invaluable contribution and sacrifice for the nation. GOC also assured them of wholehearted support to solve their problems and complimented all ranks of Fire and Fury Corps and the UT Administration for their dedicated efforts in ensuring welfare and development of veterans and their dependents. 

GOC felicitated Veterans / Veer Naris and Veer Matas from Ladakh during the event.

In 2025, more than  45 Ex-servicemen were employed through Placement Cell, Leh with the assistance of Army Welfare Placement Organisation (AWPO). More than 200 veterans and dependents were trained through the Digital Learning Centre established at Leh. To harness the potential of solar energy in Leh, more than 150 veterans were trained as solar technicians, thereby enabling them with better job opportunities. SPARSH Outreach Programs were conducted at remote locations like Nubra Valley, Nimu, Karu, Kargil and Dras to facilitate ESM, Veer Matas and Veer Naris.

Veterans Day was also celebrated at other locations in the entire Ladakh and more than 1200 veterans attended these events. 

The grand celebration stands testimony to the commitment of Fire and Fury Corps towards the welfare of veterans of Ladakh.

