Fire and Fury Corps: Nation Building

A sheep shelter constructed by the Indian Army at Rale Iching Village, Durbuk, at 15,500 ft, marks another meaningful step for the development of Ladakh under Operation Sadbhavana.

Equipped with modern heating facilities, the shelter ensures protection, warmth and proper care for livestock during Ladakh’s extreme winters.

More than an infrastructure project, this initiative strengthens community livelihoods, safeguards the local livestock based economy and reduces winter losses for nomadic and rural families by supporting traditional occupations and enhancing resilience in high-altitude areas. 

