Exercise #PRAGATI

Lieutenant General Dhiraj Seth, #VCOAS, along with Vice Chiefs and senior military leaders from participating nations, witnessed the Final Validation Exercise and Closing Ceremony of the maiden edition of Multilateral Military Exercise #PRAGATI 2026 at Umroi, Meghalaya. The event marked the successful culmination of a landmark multinational engagement.

Bringing together over 400 troops from 12 Friendly Foreign Countries, the exercise fostered camaraderie and enhanced operational synergy. Conducted in the spirit of partnership and shared responsibility, Exercise #PRAGATI reinforced the collective commitment towards peace, stability and security in the Indian Ocean Region.

Participating nations also witnessed an indigenous defence industry demonstration. It highlighted India's growing technological and defence manufacturing capabilities and underscored the nation's commitment towards #AtmanirbharBharat and indigenous solutions for future-ready military operations.

