In commemoration of the 78th United Nations Peacekeepers Day, Lieutenant General Vipul Shinghal, Deputy Chief of the Army Staff (IS&T), laid a wreath at the National War Memorial, paying tribute to the #Bravehearts who made the supreme sacrifice while serving in United Nations peacekeeping missions.

On the occasion, Dag Hammarskjöld Medals were awarded posthumously to Lance Havildar Harbhajan Singh and Naib Subedar Sujit Kumar Pradhan in honour of their exemplary courage, dedication and sacrifice in the line of duty.

Marking the occasion, the #IndianArmy also hosted a dialogue on “Future of UN Global Peacekeeping” at Manekshaw Centre, attended by Mr Stefan Priesner, Amb Ruchira Kamboj, Lieutenant General Satish Nambiar (Retd) and other senior military dignitaries, reaffirming India’s steadfast commitment towards global peace and security.

