Indian Army and M/s Air India Ltd signed a Memorandum of Cooperation (MoC) in the presence of #GeneralUpendraDwivedi, #COAS, towards further strengthening welfare initiatives for the Army fraternity.

Built on the three pillars of Employment, Empowerment and Environment, the partnership aims to create lifelong employment avenues for Veer Naris and their wards, support vocational training infrastructure in ASHA Schools and promote environment-friendly mobility solutions at Army Hospitals.

Under the initiative, 20 vacancies for Veer Naris and 40 vacancies for their wards will be provided across seven airports. In addition, vocational laboratories will be established in 25 ASHA Schools and battery-operated carts inducted at Army Hospitals to enhance patient mobility and care.

@DefenceMinIndia
@SpokespersonMoD

#GeneralUpendraDwivedi, #COAS, inaugurated a 3 Tesla MRI facility at Army Hospital (R&R), enhancing advanced diagnostic capabilities in neurology, oncology, cardiology, musculoskeletal imaging and trauma care. The #COAS then paid heartfelt tributes to the families of Organ Donors, whose selfless decision in moments of personal grief gave the priceless gift of life to patients. 

On the occasion, Dr Subhash Gupta, a renowned Hepato-biliary and Liver Transplant surgeon was awarded with COAS Commendation Card for his contribution to the success of the organ transplant program in the Armed Forces.

Emphasising the spirit of ‘Seva Parmo Dharma’, the #COAS encouraged Armed Forces personnel, veterans and civilians to pledge for organ donation. He appreciated the efforts of Armed Forces Organ Retrieval & Transplant Authority (AORTA) in promoting organ donation.

@DefenceMinIndia
@SpokespersonMoD
