Exercise #DharmaGuardian 2026

The 7th edition of Joint Military Exercise #DharmaGuardian 2026 between India and Japan will be conducted at Chaubattia, Uttarakhand from 24 February to 9 March 2026.

The aim of the exercise is to enhance interoperability between the two forces while undertaking joint urban warfare and counter-terrorism operations. Over the two weeks, troops will refine joint planning, synchronise tactical drills and practise specialised combat skills. Key activities include establishing a Temporary Operating Base, developing an ISR grid, mobile check posts, cordon and search operations, heliborne missions and house intervention drills.

#DharmaGuardian 2026 reaffirms the growing India-Japan defence partnership and shared commitment to regional security.

