Book Release by COAS

A book titled 'Red Lines Redrawn: Operation Sindoor and India’s New Normal' was released by #GeneralUpendraDwivedi, #COAS at the India International Centre, New Delhi on 22 January 2026. 

The book provides a comprehensive, multi-domain account of #OperationSindoor, detailing India’s decisive response to Pakistan-sponsored terrorism during the 88-hour campaign that redefined the nation’s approach to proxy war.

Authored by Maj Gen Bipin Bakshi (Retd), Air Mshl Rajesh Kumar (Retd), Amb Anil Trigunayat (Retd) and Brig Akhelesh Bhargava (Retd), the volume offers rare insights into strategic planning and execution across land, air, sea, cyber and diplomatic domains. The book examines India’s Dynamic Response Doctrine, with emphasis on escalation dominance, calibrated signalling and swift conflict termination as was evident during the operation.

