NCC: Nurturing Patriotism, Talent and Unity

#GeneralUpendraDwivedi, #COAS visited the National Cadet Corps (NCC) Republic Day Camp 2026 at New Delhi and reviewed the ‘Guard of Honour’ presented by the impeccably turned-out NCC cadets of the Army, Navy and Air Force wings. The visit also featured an impressive band display by the cadets of Scindia School, Gwalior, Madhya Pradesh.

During the visit, #COAS inspected the ‘Flag Area’, meticulously prepared by cadets from all 17 NCC Directorates, showcasing diverse and inspiring themes. He visited the NCC ‘Hall of Fame’, a tribute to the illustrious legacy of the National Cadet Corps and witnessed a vibrant Cultural Programme presented by the cadets, showcasing the rich diversity and heritage of Incredible India.

Addressing the cadets, #COAS fondly recalled his own days in the NCC and the valuable lessons they imparted. He emphasised that the NCC is a true “way of life”, one that shapes character, instils discipline, nurtures leadership qualities and fosters a deep sense of national pride. Encouraging the cadets to dream big, he urged them to emerge as the leaders of tomorrow. #COAS also interacted with the cadets and lauded their enthusiasm, discipline and unwavering zeal to join the #ArmedForces.

