Global effort. Shared responsibility. A safer future.

The United Nations Fellowship on Small Arms & Light Weapons, #SALW Control concluded at the Military College of Materials Management, #MCMM, Jabalpur.

18 fellows from 13 Indo-Pacific nations attended the 3 weeks intensive training. Conducted by the United Nations Office for Disarmament Affairs, #UNODA with support from the Ministry of External Affairs and Ministry of Defence, Government of India, the fellowship aimed to strengthen international cooperation and build capacity to combat the illicit proliferation of small arms and light weapons.

The closing address was delivered by Lieutenant General Sanjay Sethi, Commandant, MCMM and the vote of thanks was presented by Mr. Martinez Manuel, UNODA.

A meaningful step toward strengthening global capabilities to counter illicit weapons and promote international security.

