In a significant stride towards advancing equine excellence, the Equine Breeding Stud, Babugarh of the Remount Veterinary Corps (#RVC), has successfully embraced Assisted Reproductive Technologies, welcoming seven elite Warmblood foals. Born using imported cryopreserved semen of renowned European stallions SATISFACTION and ZINEDINE, the initiative marks a new chapter in scientific breeding.

This milestone reflects the #IndianArmy’s commitment to adopting cutting-edge technologies for genetic upgradation and achieving gold standards in equine breeding. By integrating superior global germplasm, the programme strengthens the foundation for producing high performance horses capable of excelling at national and international equestrian arenas.

A pivotal leap in enhancing the quality, endurance and competitiveness of Indian Army’s equestrian assets, reinforcing its legacy of excellence in the field. 

