In a remarkable first, Team 22 Mobile Field Veterinary Hospital, #Averipatti of #TripeaksBde successfully performed a rare and complex colic surgery on an Army mule under field conditions.

The case involved a critical 360-degree torsion of the large intestine, accurately diagnosed through ultrasonography. With time being of the essence, the veterinary team undertook a swift and decisive surgical intervention, correcting the torsion and carrying out decompression of the intestine under constrained field environment.

Demonstrating exceptional skill and commitment, the team ensured the mule’s full recovery. The animal is now active, showing no signs of discomfort, and has successfully returned to its normal operational duties.

This achievement reflects the unwavering professionalism of Army Veterinary Corps personnel in preserving the health and operational readiness of animal assets, even in the most demanding terrains.

