In a significant stride towards strengthening satellite-based communications in the Middle Sector, the #IndianArmy’s #CentralCommand has entered into a landmark partnership with Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (#BSNL) for provisioning high-speed internet services in remote and operationally challenging areas through Low Earth Orbit satellite constellation.

The MoU was signed by Maj Gen Anirudh Sakhre, #CSO HQ Central Command and Ms Indu Jaisal, GM Business Enterprise Platinum BSNL in the presence of Lt Gen Navin Sachdeva, COS HQ #SuryaCommand. This initiative marks a decisive step towards enabling resilient, beyond line-of-sight connectivity with enhanced bandwidth across diverse terrain.

The collaboration aims to strengthen operational communication, welfare connectivity and Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief support by ensuring robust network redundancy and reduced reliance on conventional terrestrial systems.

By integrating next-generation technologies with operational needs, the initiative reflects a forward-looking vision and deep synergy between the Indian Army and national telecom agencies, paving the way for a secure, agile and future-ready communication grid capable of delivering reliable connectivity anytime, anywhere and under all conditions.

