In a solemn and dignified ceremony, the #Varanasi Cantonment Board dedicated a road within the Cantonment premises as Late Capt Mukesh Srivastava, Sena Medal (Posthumous) Marg on the occasion of his 25th Death Anniversary. The road was inaugurated by his mother Mrs Sarojini Srivastava and his brother Mr Rupesh Srivastava, in the presence of officers, families of 39 Gorkha Training Centre, CEO Cantonment Board, SDM Sadar and local residents.

Commissioned into 2nd Battalion, the 3rd Gorkha Rifles (2/3 GR) and later serving with 32 RR, Capt Mukesh Srivastava displayed extraordinary bravery during a search and destroy operation in #Kupwara, J&K on 13 April 2001. Despite being struck by 13 bullets, he continued to lead and engage the terrorists for over 40 minutes, ensuring the mission’s success before making the ultimate sacrifice. He was posthumously awarded the Sena Medal for Gallantry.

This dedication stands as a lasting tribute to his indomitable courage, unwavering devotion and selfless service, an enduring inspiration for generations to uphold the highest ideals of duty, honour and sacrifice.

