"𝗦𝘁𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗴𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗻𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗙𝗶𝗿𝘀𝘁 𝗥𝗲𝘀𝗽𝗼𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗿𝘀, 𝗦𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗥𝗮𝗶𝗹 𝗡𝗲𝘁𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸𝘀."

A two-day CIED Training Cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers at Shingara Training School, #Barabanki for personnel of Railway Protection Force, as part of the Disaster Management Course at Jagjivan Ram National RPF Academy, #Lucknow.

The training focused on prevention, mitigation and response to IED threats, enhancing the capability of RPF as first responders. Trainees underwent tabke top exercises, field drills, joint exercises and hands-on practice on detection, search and response procedures.

A key highlight was the demonstration of safe removal of an IED from a railway bogey using specialised equipment and techniques. Emphasis was laid on rail bogey and platform search drills, response to suspected objects and Post Blast Investigation protocols.

Participants were also familiarised with modern equipment including bomb suits, IR cameras, detection systems and specialised vehicles, providing valuable exposure to contemporary CIED operations.
The training significantly enhanced operational preparedness and inter-agency coordination. Participants expressed high appreciation for the quality of instruction, practical exposure and professionalism of the Indian Army.

