Commemorating the 262nd #ArmyMedicalCorps Day, a spirited #Cycle Expedition was organised by AMC C&C, #Lucknow. The 160 km expedition from #Lucknow to #RaeBareli was flagged off by Maj Gen V K Ratan (Retd) at HQ AMC C&C, symbolising endurance, resilience and the unwavering ethos of service.

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand and Lt Gen Shivinder Singh, Comdt AMC C&C, OIC Records & Col Comdt AMC, joined the expedition, inspiring all ranks through their presence and leadership.

Led by Maj Gen KJ Singh, Dy Comdt & CI, a dedicated team of 17 AMC Officers and JCOs/OR are undertaking this two-day journey, strengthening bonds of camaraderie, promoting physical fitness and reaffirming commitment to the nation.

The expedition stands as a tribute to the indomitable spirit of the #ArmyMedicalCorps, ever ready to serve, heal and protect.

