A two-day Counter IED Training Cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers at #Barabanki for personnel of the Railway Protection Force, #Lucknow, as part of their Disaster Management Course at Jagjivan Ram National RPF Academy.

43 trainees, including Inspectors, Sub Inspectors, ASIs and other ranks from Eastern & North Western Railway Divisions, underwent intensive training. The programme covered prevention, mitigation and response to IED threats with focus on railway-specific scenarios.

Training included table-top exercises, group discussions, field drills, joint exercises, equipment practicals and live demonstrations. A key highlight was the safe removal of an IED from a railway bogey using specialised techniques and equipment.

Participants were introduced to modern equipment including Bomb Suits, IR cameras, explosive and narcotics detectors, search tools and specialised mobility platforms, enhancing their technological awareness and operational readiness.

The training significantly strengthened capacity building at the grassroots level and fostered inter-agency coordination. The programme received high appreciation from participants for its practical orientation, quality of instruction and exposure to specialised capabilities of the Indian Army.

