Displaying prompt response and professional excellence, #IndiaArmy swiftly mobilised an Emergency Response Team of COD #Prayagraj following the cold storage collapse and ammonia gas leak near Phaphamau on 23 Mar 2026.

Rescue team integrated seamlessly with NDRF and civil administration, establishing a safety cordon and supporting rescue efforts in a highly hazardous environment. Continuous water spraying using TFF was undertaken to reduce ammonia concentration, enabling safer debris clearance and sustained operations.

Despite challenging conditions, including toxic gas exposure and risk of trapped personnel, the Emergency Response Team ensured effective coordination, hazard mitigation and operational safety at site.

The team remained deployed for extended hours, stabilising the situation before safely disengaging. Additional teams remain on standby to respond to any contingency, reaffirming unwavering commitment towards HADR and support to civil authorities.

