Four days of relentless energy, discipline and determination culminated in a grand finale at the Central Command Athletic Championship 2026 held at Mathew Ground, 1 STC, #Jabalpur.

The championship stood as a true testament to the indomitable spirit of the Indian Army, where every stride reflected resilience, every finish line marked progress and every participant embodied the ethos of sportsmanship. From record-breaking feats to inspiring displays of teamwork, the event celebrated not just competition but the pursuit of excellence.

The vibrant pipe band performances by Signallers and Grenadiers added a stirring rhythm to the occasion, echoing pride, precision and tradition. The presence of distinguished sportspersons, Sub Kunhu Mohammed (Olympian 2016) and Sub Maj (Hony Capt) KS Mathew (Head Coach, Indian Marathon Team – 2012 Olympics), further elevated the significance of the championship, inspiring participants to aim higher and push beyond limits.

As the championship concludes, it leaves behind more than medals and records. It leaves a legacy of grit, unity and an enduring commitment to excellence. A fitting culmination to a remarkable sporting spectacle.

