A 5 Ton Integrated Sanitation Park was inaugurated at #VaranasiCantt, transforming a previously neglected landfill into a 1.4 acre state of the art waste management facility.

The solar powered complex is equipped with modern infrastructure for dry and wet waste processing, composting and dry waste upcycling. It also incorporates rainwater harvesting, a weigh bridge, waste collection vehicle washing and parking area, dedicated training and workshop spaces, along with accommodation for Safai Sathis.

Developed as a CSR initiative by #SBIFoundation in collaboration with #FeedbackFoundation, the facility was inaugurated by  
Maj Gen Amit Singh Sohal, #GOC, Purva UP & MP Sub Area,  in the presence of senior officials. The initiative reflects the Indian Army’s continued commitment to sustainable practices, environmental responsibility and active community participation in line with the vision of #SwachhBharat.

