The #IndianArmy participated in Technex’26 Defence Symposium 2.0 at IIT (BHU) #Varanasi under the aegis of #SuryaCommand, engaging with students, innovators and academia to discuss the future of defence technology and military-civil fusion.

Maj Gen Amit Singh Sohal, #GOC, Purva UP & MP Sub Area, addressed the gathering and highlighted the Army’s vision for technology driven transformation. The interaction focused on the #DecadeOfTransformation and #YearofNetworkingAndDataCentricity 2026, emphasising the expanding role of emerging technologies including drones, AI, cyber capabilities and autonomous systems in shaping future warfare.

The symposium also reinforced the vision of #AtmanirbharBharat, encouraging collaboration between the Army, academia and startups through initiatives such as the Army Design Bureau and the Compendium of Problem Statements to develop indigenous solutions for national security.

An equipment display by the #IndianArmy showcased nano, micro and large drones, weapons, radio sets, night vision devices, warfare vehicles, robot mules and guns, providing students a closer look at evolving battlefield technologies.

