Strengthening inter-agency cooperation and operational preparedness, a three-day Counter-IED Training Cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers for personnel of #SashastraSeemaBal at the Shingara Training School, #Barabanki, with 42 trainees including two officers participating.

The cadre covered a comprehensive range of modules including table-top exercises, group discussions, field drills, joint exercises, classroom sessions and hands-on equipment practice. The focus remained on drills, response protocols and safety procedures while dealing with suspected objects, IED awareness and identification of suspicious indicators during operations.

Participants were also introduced to IED mechanisms and field-based practical demonstrations, along with familiarisation of modern Counter-IED equipment such as Scorpio-based JX platform, modified ALS, IR cameras, bomb suits, explosives & narcotics detectors and specialised search and detection systems.

The programme received excellent feedback from all participants, who appreciated the quality of instruction, demonstrations and exposure to specialised equipment, many of which they experienced for the first time during such training. Such initiatives continue to strengthen capacity building, preparedness and seamless inter-agency cooperation in dealing with emerging security challenges.

