Military Hospital #Fatehgarh successfully conducted a NCC Medical Attachment Camp, for cadets of 13 UP Girls’ Battalion and 37 UP Boys’ Battalion, #Ghaziabad.

Over 54 NCC cadets underwent hands-on training in Basic Life Support, mannequin-based CPR, ABC protocols, burn management, medical equipment handling and the basics of drone usage, equipping them with essential life-saving skills and emergency response awareness.

The camp blended learning with camaraderie as cadets celebrated Holi with hospital staff, participated in painting and drawing competitions and strengthened bonds through interactive activities. All participants were awarded Certificates of Participation.

The initiative reflects #IndianArmy's commitment towards youth empowerment, skill development and nation building, while inspiring the next generation to serve with knowledge, compassion and responsibility. 

