Ms Asha Malviya, a national level athlete, mountaineer and solo cyclist known for undertaking a 7,800 km nationwide cycling expedition promoting Women Empowerment and Nation Empowerment, met Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand, at #Lucknow.

Commencing her remarkable journey on 11 Jan 2026 from #Jaipur on the occasion of #IndianArmyDay, she is cycling from the westernmost region of India to #Kibithu in #ArunachalPradesh, the easternmost frontier of the nation. Having already covered nearly 3,700 km across #Rajasthan, #Gujarat and #MadhyaPradesh, her mission reflects courage, determination and an indomitable spirit.

During her visit, #ArmyCdr cycled alongside Ms Malviya in #Lucknow, encouraging her inspiring mission and acknowledging her efforts to promote women empowerment, patriotism and resilience through endurance cycling. She also interacted with students of #APSLBSMarg, sharing experiences from her journey and motivating young minds to pursue their dreams with discipline, confidence and determination. The interaction encouraged students to embrace challenges with courage and strive for excellence in every field.

Her expedition continues towards the eastern frontiers of the country, carrying a powerful message of empowerment, perseverance and national pride. The #IndianArmy and #CentralCommand extend their best wishes for the successful completion of her inspiring journey. 

