A one day Counter Improvised Explosive Device (#CIED) training cadre was conducted by 201 CEDU at Shingara Training School, Barabanki for 42 trainees of the #RailwayProtectionForce undergoing Disaster Management Course at Jagjivan Ram National RPF Academy, #Lucknow.

The training covered prevention, mitigation and response to IED related threats with a focus on the role of RPF as first responders in railway security scenarios. Trainees from Eastern Railway Division participated in table-top exercises, group discussions, field drills, joint exercises and practical sessions on detection, search and response procedures.

The training emphasised drills for rail bogey and platform searches, response protocols on detection of suspected objects and procedures for Post Blast Investigation. The initiative significantly contributed to operational capacity building and strengthened inter agency coordination between the #IndianArmy and #RPF.

Participants appreciated the practical exposure, demonstrations and professional instruction by the unit, noting the training as highly valuable for enhancing technological awareness and preparedness in dealing with IED related contingencies. 

