Demonstrating exceptional airborne skill and operational precision, the #ShatrujeetWarriors carried out high-risk water Para Jumps at #TehriDam, executing both Static Line and Combat Freefall insertions as part of a specialised airborne training exercise.

Simulating a high-altitude lake insertion, the complex operation demanded meticulous planning, flawless coordination and precise execution. The paratroopers descended with remarkable accuracy into the challenging waters of Tehri, showcasing their mastery in airborne operations and their readiness to undertake specialised missions in demanding terrain.

The exercise also highlighted the strong joint synergy between the #IndianArmy and the #IndianAirForce, reflecting the growing emphasis on integrated training and seamless cooperation in modern operations.
Through such rigorous training, the Shatrujeet Warriors continue to uphold the elite traditions of India’s airborne forces, reinforcing operational preparedness, combat effectiveness and the spirit of excellence that defines the Indian Army.

