Under the aegis of Station Headquarters #Varanasi, troops joined hands with the civil administration and Municipal Corporation in a landmark plantation drive at Sujabad–Domri, scripting a historic green milestone for Kashi.

In a remarkable collective effort, over 2.5 lakh saplings were planted in just one hour. As a dedicated military contribution, 250 soldiers from Varanasi Military Station planted 10,000 trees with unmatched josh and discipline, reaffirming the Indian Army’s commitment beyond the battlefield.

The initiative strengthens the ecological shield along the Ganga riverfront and reinforces shared resolve towards climate resilience and sustainable development. Participation of families, NCC cadets, school children and citizens transformed the drive into a true जनआंदोलन for the environment.
Varanasi did not just plant trees today. It planted hope for generations to come. 

