A focused knowledge session on emerging operational dynamics and capability optimisation was conducted at Nanda Sunanda Auditorium, fostering informed perspectives and institutional preparedness.

Lt Gen Navin Sachdeva, Chief of Staff, HQ #CentralCommand delivered an insightful address on “Perspective on Northern Adversary & Collusivity”, highlighting evolving security paradigms, multi-domain challenges and the strategic implications of collusive threats along the Northern borders. The session provided valuable operational clarity and reinforced the importance of integrated readiness, adaptive planning and jointness in the contemporary security environment.

This was followed by a detailed presentation by Shri Hari Har Mishrs, #IDAS, #IFA,  #CentralCommand on “Economy of Drone Purchases”, focusing on cost-effective capability development, procurement prudence and optimisation of unmanned aerial systems within operational and fiscal frameworks. The deliberation underscored the growing relevance of drones in modern warfare and the need to balance technological advancement with financial sustainability.

The session strengthened professional military understanding while aligning operational priorities with future-ready capability building.

