Demonstrating unwavering readiness in aid to civil authorities, HQ J&B Sub Area, #Danapur participated in a State Level Earthquake Mock Exercise conducted on in coordination with the Bihar State Disaster Management Agency, District Administration, #NDRF, #SDRF and emergency response services.

Seven specialised response teams from the Bihar Regimental Centre, along with medical teams each from Military Hospital Danapur and Military Hospital #Gaya, actively participated in both the Table Top Exercise (TTX) and the integrated Mock Drill. The exercise validated inter-agency coordination, rapid response mechanisms, casualty evacuation drills and disaster mitigation protocols in a simulated earthquake scenario.

The participation reinforced the Indian Army’s steadfast commitment towards humanitarian assistance and disaster relief operations, ensuring swift, coordinated and effective response in times of crisis while strengthening synergy with civil administration and disaster management agencies.

