Pashchim UP Sub Area, in collaboration with #PineDivision and #RamDivision, successfully organised the “Know Your Army Mela” at Kulwant Singh Stadium, #MeerutCantt, fostering deeper awareness about the Indian Army among the youth. Approximately 4,500 students from 51 schools across Meerut and adjoining regions participated with great enthusiasm. The event aimed to familiarise young minds with the Army’s role, operational capabilities and diverse career opportunities, while nurturing patriotism and national pride.

A comprehensive display of military equipment and combat support systems formed the highlight of the mela. Infantry weapons, armour platforms, mobile bridging systems, medical assets and other operational gear were showcased, offering students a close look at the Army’s technological and operational prowess. Army canines, equestrian demonstrations and a stirring performance by the Army Band added energy and vibrancy to the occasion. Interactive engagements with serving personnel enabled students to understand the functioning of various arms and services and gain insights into the life, values and ethos of the Armed Forces, inspiring many towards future service.

The #GOC, Pashchim UP Sub Area, attended the event as Chief Guest. Interacting warmly with the children, he encouraged them to strive for excellence and uphold the ideals of discipline, integrity and dedication. The mela concluded as a resounding success, strengthening civil–military connect and leaving a lasting impression on the nation’s future torchbearers.

