A significant step towards restoring #Lucknow’s lifeline was taken at the Strategic Conclave on #GomtiRiver Rejuvenation hosted by the #UttarPradesh State Transformation Commission under the theme Revitalizing the Lifeline: Clean Gomti. The high-level forum brought together policymakers, environmental experts and development partners to chart a coordinated path for sustainable river management.

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand and Lt Gen Navin Sachdeva, Chief of Staff #CentralCommand, underlined the importance of military-civil synergy, institutional cohesion and community participation in restoring fragile riverine ecosystems.

 In his address, the #ArmyCdr emphasised that environmental stability and a healthier climate directly enhance operational preparedness. Cleaner river systems, improved terrain conditions and ecological balance contribute to better mobility, sustainability and overall effectiveness of troops in diverse operational environments.

The discussions highlighted the Territorial Army’s Ecological Task Forces whose disciplined and sustained field efforts across the country remain a benchmark in river rejuvenation, afforestation and terrain restoration. With participation from global partners including the World Bank and Asian Development Bank, the conclave forged a unified roadmap to secure a cleaner, healthier Gomti for future generations.

