Strengthening institutional synergy and advancing soldier welfare, Maj Gen Vikas Bhardwaj, #GOC Jharkhand & Bihar Sub Area, led a delegation for a high-level interaction at the office of the Hon’ble Deputy Chief Minister of #Bihar, Shri Samrat Chaudhary. The meeting was conducted as a follow-up to the earlier engagement.

The civil administration delegation, led by the Hon’ble Dy CM, included the Chief Secretary, DGP, DG Ops, ACS Home, Secretary Land & Revenue, and representatives from the State Urban Development and Irrigation Departments, reflecting a whole-of-government approach towards issues concerning the #ArmedForces community.

Key matters deliberated included welfare and resettlement of Veterans and Veeranganas, alongside the need for a proactive and responsive grievance redress mechanism for serving as well as retired personnel. Discussions also focused on management of Defence land and infrastructure development, aimed at enhancing coordination and enabling structured Military–Civil fusion across the state.

The interaction underscored growing convergence between the Army and the State Administration, strengthening mutual understanding on priority issues. The Hon’ble Dy CM appreciated the immense contributions of the Armed Forces fraternity and assured full support towards welfare initiatives, timely grievance resolution and inclusive engagement with soldiers, veterans and their families across #Bihar.

