Under the aegis of HQ Purva UP & MP Sub Area, an Ex-Servicemen Multi-Speciality Medical Camp was successfully conducted by Military Hospital, #Prayagraj, reaffirming the Indian Army’s steadfast commitment to the health and welfare of its Veterans.

Recognising the evolving healthcare needs of Ex-Servicemen, especially in preventive screening, specialist consultation and early diagnosis, the initiative brought comprehensive, multi-disciplinary medical care closer to those who once served the Nation with dedication. Over 500 Veterans benefited from integrated specialist consultations and treatment under one roof.

Specialist teams from Orthopaedics, Ophthalmology, ENT, Cardiology and Physiotherapy conducted focused screenings, treatment and preventive health counselling. A key highlight of the camp was Basic Life Support (BLS) training, where Veterans were trained in CPR techniques, management of choking, early recognition of cardiac arrest and stroke symptoms, safe casualty handling, recovery position and activation of emergency medical response.

The initiative strengthened community-level emergency preparedness and reaffirmed the Army’s unwavering commitment to the continued health, welfare and well-being of its Veterans.

