“Train Hard. Save Lives. Fight Strong.”

In alignment with the directives and Key Result Areas laid down by the #COAS, Officers Training College, AMC Centre & College successfully conducted a 3-day Yodha Rakshak Combat Casualty Care (YRCCC) capsule for combatants of 71 Mountain Brigade.

The intensive training integrated expert lectures with realistic hands-on drills on advanced manikins, equipping participants with critical battlefield lifesaving competencies. A total of 577 personnel including 20 Officers, 58 Junior Commissioned Officers and 499 Other Ranks underwent structured training focused on immediate trauma response in combat environments.

Combatants were trained in massive haemorrhage control, effective tourniquet application, wound packing and other essential Combat Casualty Care protocols, reinforcing survivability in high-risk operational settings. The capsule stands as a force multiplier, empowering frontline warriors to preserve life while sustaining mission effectiveness.

