Uttarakhand’s Lok Bhavan hosted the Bharat Himalayan Strategy Forum, bringing together senior military leadership and strategic experts to deliberate on the evolving security and geopolitical dynamics of the Himalayan region.

The forum was attended by Hon’ble Governor Lt Gen Gurmeet Singh (Retd), Chief of Defence Staff Gen Anil Chauhan and Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand. The event commenced with a traditional lamp-lighting ceremony.

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta addressed the gathering, highlighting the strategic significance of the Himalayan frontier, the imperative of integrated preparedness and the role of civil-military synergy in addressing emerging security challenges across the region.

On the occasion, the Hon’ble Governor inaugurated the BHISHMA website, expanding India’s strategic research and digital knowledge outreach. Bharat Himalayan International Strategic Manch (BHISM) is a premier Indian think tank fostering research and discourse on India’s development, geopolitics, economic security, cultural depth and defence strategy, with focus on the Himalayan frontier.

