“𝗛𝗼𝗻𝗼𝘂𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗩𝗮𝗹𝗼𝘂𝗿, 𝗣𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗟𝗲𝗴𝗮𝗰𝘆, 𝗜𝗻𝘀𝗽𝗶𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀.”

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand, visited the under-construction Trishul Raksha Sanghralaya at #Moradabad, witnessing firsthand the steady progress of this landmark nation-building initiative. 

The visit highlighted the #IndianArmy’s continued commitment towards preserving military heritage and strengthening military-civil connect through institutional memory and public outreach.

During the visit, the #Army Cdr interacted with Mr AK Singh, #IAS, Divisional Commissioner, and Mr Devyanshu Patel, IAS, Municipal Commissioner. He commended their collective vision and administrative resolve in shaping the museum into a world-class centre that will reflect the गौरवगाथा of India’s Armed Forces and their timeless contribution to national security.

Envisioned as a dynamic knowledge and inspiration hub, the Trishul Raksha Sanghralaya will showcase rare war artefacts, vintage weapon systems, archival records, immersive galleries and interactive war-room experiences. The museum will chronicle defining battles, operational triumphs and stories of supreme sacrifice, offering citizens, youth and researchers a powerful window into the ethos of soldiering.

More than a repository of history, the #Sanghralaya will stand as a living tribute to courage, leadership and patriotism, igniting pride, deepening awareness and inspiring future generations to connect with the legacy of India’s #ArmedForces.

#IndianArmy #SuryaCommand #NationBuilding #VeerGatha #TrishulMuseum

