On the occasion of International Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery Day, #CentralCommand Military Dental Centre  organised a comprehensive Road Safety and Prevention of Maxillofacial Injuries Awareness Programme, reinforcing the critical link between responsible road behaviour and facial trauma prevention.

A focused lecture was delivered highlighting the life-saving importance of helmets and seat belts, safe riding practices and adherence to traffic regulations. The session featured a special address by Raghvendra Kumar, widely known as the “Helmet Man of India,” whose grassroots road safety campaign has inspired behavioural change across communities.

The programme was conducted at Army Public School, LBS Marg, engaging over 200 students from Classes VIII, IX and XI through interactive discussions and safety demonstrations aimed at building early awareness among youth.

Extending the outreach, an evening lecture was organised at the AMC Auditorium, attended by 100 MOBC Officers and 300 recruits, emphasising operational responsibility, personal safety and long-term health implications of maxillofacial injuries.

Through education, engagement and advocacy, the initiative effectively advanced awareness on road safety while promoting preventive measures to reduce facial trauma, reaffirming the Armed Forces’ commitment towards community health and responsible citizenship.

#IndianArmy #SuryaCommand #RoadSafety #OralSurgeryDay #SafetyFirst 

