HQ #CentralCommand showcased its commitment to environmental stewardship and aesthetic excellence by participating in the Annual Flower Show organised at #Rajbhavan
#Lucknow from 06–09 Feb 2026. Competing alongside premier government institutions, the formation earned top honours and wide appreciation for its lush greenery and vibrant seasonal displays.

The prizes were distributed by Mr B L Meena, IAS, Addl Chief Secretary, Department of Horticulture, Sericulture and Food Processing, #UttarPradesh.

In Category I (Flower Pots with Seasonal Flowers), HQ Central Command competed across 88 entries and delivered an exceptional performance, securing 20 First positions, 10 Second positions and 19 Third positions, taking the total podium finishes to an impressive 49.

In Category II (Lawns of Government Departments), the formation’s horticultural excellence was further recognised with Central Lawn and Front Lawn both securing First position, while the Engr Lawn earned Second position, reflecting consistent landscaping standards across locations.

The achievement reflects meticulous planning, sustained horticultural effort and a deep commitment towards maintaining eco-friendly, vibrant military campuses that inspire pride and wellbeing.

