A two-day Counter Improvised Explosive Device (CIED) Training Cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers for personnel of the Railway Protection Force at Shingara Training School, #Barabanki.

The cadre formed part of the Disaster Management Course underway at Jagjivan Ram National RPF Academy, #Lucknow, the RPF’s premier national training establishment.

A total of 42 RPF trainees underwent intensive training covering table-top exercises, group discussions, classroom sessions, field drills, joint exercises and hands-on equipment practicals. 

A major highlight was the live demonstration on safe neutralisation and removal of an IED from a railway bogey employing specialised equipment, drills and safety protocols.

The initiative marked a significant step towards enhancing operational preparedness, strengthening capacity building and fostering effective inter-agency coordination in counter-IED operations.

