#MilitaryHospitalMhow conducted “#ExRahaat”, a comprehensive mock disaster management drill on 02 Feb 2026 to assess and practise the hospital’s disaster management plan. The exercise was carried out in close coordination with Station HQ Mhow, Station Units, Civil Administrative Authorities, Civil Police, local government agencies and the Red Cross Hospital.

The joint exercise tested critical emergency response procedures including evacuation, triage and treatment protocols, ensuring seamless coordination among all participating stakeholders. Realistic scenarios enabled medical and support teams to respond under simulated high-pressure conditions.

The drill validated existing disaster response mechanisms, identified areas for improvement and reinforced overall preparedness, reaffirming the commitment of #AFMS and the #IndianArmy to patient safety and an effective response during real-life emergencies.

