As part of the Disaster Management Course at Jagjivan Ram National RPF Academy #Lucknow, a two day CIED training cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers at Shingara Training School #Barabanki for Railway Protection Force personnel.

The training focused on prevention mitigation and response to IED related incidents with emphasis on RPF’s role as first responders in rail environments. A total of 41 trainees from South Eastern Central Railway divisions including officers and other ranks participated.

The cadre included table top exercises field drills equipment practicals and live demonstrations including safe removal of an IED from a railway bogey. Rail bogey and platform search drills actions on suspected objects and Post Blast Investigation procedures were practised with strict safety protocols.

Modern equipment including bomb suits IR cameras detection equipment and specialised vehicles were demonstrated. The training greatly enhanced operational readiness technological awareness and inter agency coordination and was highly appreciated by participants for its realism and quality of instruction.

