#SuryaCommand marks the 78th #ArmyDay remembering the historic moment in 1949 when Field Marshal KM Cariappa assumed charge as the first Indian Commander-in-Chief. The milestone signalled a new era for the Army founded on national leadership, strong professional ethos and unwavering loyalty to the Constitution.

Army Day celebrates the spirit of the Indian soldier whose courage discipline and steadfast resolve remain central to safeguarding national security. It honours generations who have stood firm in peace and in conflict always placing duty above self in service of the Nation.

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta, GOC-in-C #CentralCommand along with all ranks paid heartfelt homage to the #Bravehearts at a solemn ceremony at Kiranti War Memorial, reaffirming the Army’s enduring bond with those who made the supreme sacrifice.

Later in the day the Army Commander interacted with all ranks conveying Army Day greetings and urging them to draw inspiration from the sacrifices of the #FallenHeroes. Veterans were also felicitated as a mark of respect for their courage sacrifice and lifelong service to the Nation.

The occasion underscored the Indian Army’s commitment to uphold its proud legacy while remaining prepared resolute and future ready in the service of the Nation.

#IndianArmy #CentralCommand #ArmyDay2026 #CourageAndSacrifice #ServiceBeforeSelf #NationFirst #SaluteToSoldiers

