The 10th Armed Forces Veterans Day was commemorated with pride, solemnity and gratitude through a Mega Veterans’ Rally at Surya Auditorium, #Lucknow, organised under the aegis of Headquarters Madhya Uttar Pradesh Sub Area(#MUPSA). The event paid tribute to the selfless service, sacrifices and enduring legacy of India’s veterans.

Graced by Hon’ble Union Minister of State Prof. S. P. Singh Baghel, the rally saw heartfelt interactions with veterans and Veer Naris, who were formally felicitated in recognition of their courage, sacrifice and lifelong service to the nation. The presence of Lt Gen Navin Sachdeva, Chief of Staff, HQ #CentralCommand and Shri L. Venkateswarlu, IAS, Additional Chief Secretary (Social Welfare & Sainik Kalyan), Government of Uttar Pradesh, highlighted strong civil–military synergy in matters of veteran welfare.

Over 700 veterans and Veer Naris participated in the rally. Integrated welfare support included grievance redressal counters, ECHS assistance, medical facilities and guidance on entitlements and welfare schemes. The event reaffirmed that while soldiers may retire from active service, their contribution to nation building remains eternal and continues to inspire generations.

