"𝗦𝘁𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗴𝘁𝗵𝗲𝗻𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗙𝗶𝗿𝘀𝘁 𝗥𝗲𝘀𝗽𝗼𝗻𝗱𝗲𝗿 𝗥𝗲𝗮𝗱𝗶𝗻𝗲𝘀𝘀"

A three day Counter IED training cadre was conducted by #SuryaDisposers, Bomb Detection and Disposal Squad in collaboration with Suraksha Shakha UP Police at #Barabanki.

Thirty personnel representing all BDDS teams across Uttar Pradesh participated. The training covered table top exercises, group discussions field, joint exercises, equipment practicals and focused classes.
Realistic demonstrations included safe removal of IEDs from public locations such as banks post offices and crowded open areas using specialised equipment and proven techniques.

Key focus areas included drills actions and response of BDDS as first responders with emphasis on crowded area searches RSP procedures suspected object handling and post blast investigation. Special attention was given to safety protocols during live operational scenarios.

The cadre significantly contributed to operational capacity building and inter agency coordination and was widely appreciated by participants as a professional and impactful training initiative.

