#GoldenKeyDivision successfully conducted a strategic seminar on “Fortifying Himalayas: A Proactive Military–Civil Fusion Strategy in the Middle Sector” at Clement Town Dehradun. The seminar highlighted that safeguarding critical mountain regions requires sustained preparedness, deep integration and a long-term strategic vision.

Deliberations centered on a whole-of-nation approach bringing together robust military preparedness, resilient civil infrastructure, responsive governance and empowered community participation. Discussions emphasised seamless coordination among civil administration, Armed Forces and local stakeholders to address evolving security requirements and developmental challenges.

The event was also graced by the Hon’ble Governor of Uttarakhand Lt Gen Gurmit Singh and the Hon’ble Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami reflecting strong civil leadership support for military–civil synergy in the region.

Lt Gen Anindya Sengupta GOC-in-C #CentralCommand commended the strategic insights shared and reaffirmed the Indian Army’s commitment to close military–civil integration as a key pillar for long-term security, stability and national resilience.

