Maj Gen Vikas Bhardwaj, #GOC Jharkhand and Bihar Sub Area attended the XVII State Managing Committee Meeting presided over by the Hon’ble Governor of #Jharkhand Shri Santosh Kumar Gangwar at Lok Bhawan #Ranchi. The forum discussed practical cooperation between the Army and the state administration to strengthen policies for #VeerNaris, veterans and their dependents with special attention on grievance redress and easier access to existing welfare schemes.

The #GOC highlighted the need for focused measures such as resettlement guidance skill training medical support through #ECHS and local outreach programmes so that families of former soldiers receive timely help. Officers from various departments shared updates on ongoing initiatives and explored better use of state resources during emergencies and infrastructure projects.

After the session Maj Gen Vikas Bhardwaj had a brief interaction with the Hon’ble Governor and apprised him of Army driven efforts across the region. He thanked the Governor for his concern for serving soldiers veterans and Veer Naris and reiterated the resolve to deepen military civil partnership in Jharkhand. 

